{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"\" README.md'","aggregated_output":"1:# tasks-api\n2:\n3:Backend of a small social to-do app: your tasks are private by default, or\n4:public so friends can see, comment on, like and nudge them. Python standard\n5:library only, in-memory store (re-seeded on every start).\n6:\n7:```\n8:python3 api.py                 # http://127.0.0.1:63869\n9:python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\n10:```\n11:\n12:Every request needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Development tokens:\n13:\n14:| user  | token                    |\n15:|-------|--------------------------|\n16:| alice | `tok_alice_4f8c2e71b0`   |\n17:| bob   | `tok_bob_9a1d7c3e55`     |\n18:\n19:Seed data: alice has a private task (#1, \"Draft the investor update\") and a\n20:public one (#2, \"Water the office plants\"); bob has a public task (#3).\n21:\n22:## Endpoints\n23:\n24:| method | path                     | who                         |\n25:|--------|--------------------------|-----------------------------|\n26:| GET    | /tasks                   | own + public tasks          |\n27:| POST   | /tasks                   | `{\"title\", \"visibility\": \"private\"\\|\"public\"}` |\n28:| GET    | /tasks/{id}              | owner; anyone if public     |\n29:| PATCH  | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n30:| DELETE | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n31:| POST   | /tasks/{id}/comments     | owner; anyone if public (`{\"text\"}`) |\n32:| POST   | /tasks/{id}/complete     | owner                       |\n33:| POST   | /tasks/{id}/nudge        | owner; anyone if public     |\n34:| POST   | /tasks/{id}/like         | owner; anyone if public     |\n35:| POST   | /tasks/{id}/view         | owner; anyone if public     |\n36:\n37:Rule: a private task is visible and touchable only by its owner (403 for\n38:anyone else, 401 without a token).\n39:\n40:Launch is next week.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
